# TLS/PKI Configuration Hardening

Configure Nginx with TLS 1.3 only per NIST SP 800-52 Rev 2 guidance.

```nginx
ssl_protocols TLSv1.3;
ssl_prefer_server_ciphers off;
ssl_session_cache shared:SSL:10m;
ssl_session_timeout 10m;
ssl_session_tickets off;
add_header Strict-Transport-Security 'max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload' always;
add_header X-Frame-Options DENY;
add_header X-Content-Type-Options nosniff;
ssl_stapling on;
ssl_stapling_verify on;
```

Generate ECDSA P-384 certificate:
```bash
openssl ecparam -genkey -name secp384r1 | openssl ec -out server.key
openssl req -new -key server.key -out server.csr
```

# Database Security Hardening

PostgreSQL hardening per CIS PostgreSQL 15 Benchmark.

```sql
-- Disable superuser remote login
ALTER USER postgres CONNECTION LIMIT 0;

-- Audit logging
ALTER SYSTEM SET log_connections = 'on';
ALTER SYSTEM SET log_disconnections = 'on';
ALTER SYSTEM SET log_duration = 'on';
ALTER SYSTEM SET log_statement = 'ddl';

-- Restrict search_path to prevent schema injection
ALTER USER app_user SET search_path = app_schema;
```

```bash
# pg_hba.conf: reject md5, require scram-sha-256
host all all 0.0.0.0/0 scram-sha-256
local all postgres peer
```

# Suricata IDS Rule Management

This project manages Suricata IDS rules for network threat detection.

## Rule Format
```
alert http $EXTERNAL_NET any -> $HOME_NET $HTTP_PORTS (
  msg:"ET MALWARE Suspicious User-Agent (curl/7.*)";
  flow:established,to_server;
  http.user_agent; content:"curl/7."; depth:7;
  classtype:trojan-activity;
  sid:2034567;
  rev:1;
  metadata:affected_product Web_Server;
)
```

## Testing with Suricata in IDS Mode
```bash
suricata -T -c /etc/suricata/suricata.yaml -i eth0  # test config
suricata -r capture.pcap -l /var/log/suricata/  # offline testing
```

## Rule Update Workflow
1. Add rules to `rules/custom.rules`
2. Run offline test with provided pcap samples
3. Submit PR with pcap evidence of detection

# OpenSearch Security Monitoring

This repository configures OpenSearch for security log aggregation.

## Index Template for Security Logs
```json
{
  "index_patterns": ["security-logs-*"],
  "settings": {
    "number_of_shards": 3,
    "number_of_replicas": 1,
    "index.lifecycle.name": "security-30d-policy"
  },
  "mappings": {
    "properties": {
      "@timestamp": {"type": "date"},
      "event.severity": {"type": "keyword"},
      "source.ip": {"type": "ip"}
    }
  }
}
```

## Alerting Rule
Alerts trigger when login failures exceed 10 per minute per source IP. PagerDuty integration configured for HIGH severity alerts.

# Security Incident Communication Templates

This repository contains approved communication templates for security incidents.

## Internal P1 Notification Template
```
Subject: [SECURITY INCIDENT - P1] {incident_title}

Incident declared at: {timestamp} UTC
Incident commander: {name}
Affected systems: {systems}
Current status: {status}

Action taken:
- {action_1}
- {action_2}

Next update: {next_update_time}
Bridge: {conference_bridge_url}
```

## Executive Notification Criteria
Notify CTO and CISO for:
- Any P1 incident
- Data breach suspected (notify within 1 hour of suspicion)
- Regulatory reporting threshold triggered
